{
  "id": "COMPOUND:21580 - PROTEIN:5805",
  "verbalization": "Tomentosanol D appears to have a potential mechanism of action that involves targeting multiple downstream pathways leading to SCCH-26. The evidence suggests that Tomentosanol D acts as a target for DMS-273 and SQ20B, which in turn are targets of Malvidin 3-rutinoside-5-glucoside and beta-Cuprenene, respectively. These compounds are implicated in the regulation of SCCH-26, a cancer cell line, through their respective mechanisms. The integration of these pathways implies that Tomentosanol D may exert its effects by modulating the activity of these intermediaries, potentially influencing cellular processes that are critical for SCCH-26 survival. The observed scores in the paths suggest a plausible, though not fully elucidated, relationship between Tomentosanol D and SCCH-26, supported by a chain of targets that are biologically relevant to the disease. The mechanism is supported by the presence of a well-defined chain of targets, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully characterized.",
